    "# Part 2: Represent Categories and Lock One Split\n",
    "\n",
    "A tree needs numeric inputs, but the mushroom letters are labels. One-hot encoding creates an indicator for each observed category without inventing an order.\n",
    "\n",
    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/without_claude.png\" alt=\"Without Claude\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Without Claude: What Must Be Coordinated?\n",
    "\n",
    "The workflow must:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. separate the response before encoding;\n",
    "2. treat `?` as missing;\n",
    "3. stratify the train-test split;\n",
    "4. learn imputation and categories from training data only;\n",
    "5. handle a category that appears only in the test set;\n",
    "6. retain generated feature names for the tree plot.\n",
    "\n",
    "A pipeline protects these steps from becoming misaligned.\n"
   ]
