    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/claude_task.png\" alt=\"Claude Task\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Claude Coding Task 2: Build the Representation and Split\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Using mushrooms, write one Jupyter Notebook code cell that:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. replaces the literal ? with a missing value in the predictors;\n",
    "2. maps class e to 0 and class p to 1;\n",
    "3. creates one 80/20 stratified split with random_state = 1099;\n",
    "4. creates a preprocessing pipeline with SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")\n",
    "   and OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=False);\n",
    "5. does not fit the preprocessor separately and does not inspect test outcomes;\n",
    "6. prints train and test shapes and class proportions;\n",
    "7. names the objects X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test, and categorical_preprocessor.\n",
    "\n",
    "Return only the Python code.\n",
    "```\n",
