    "# Part 3: Fit and Interpret a Shallow Classification Tree\n",
    "\n",
    "A shallow tree is useful for learning because its rules can be plotted. `max_depth=3` is a teaching constraint, not a claim that depth three is optimal.\n",
    "\n",
    "The predicted probability at a leaf is the training-class proportion among observations that reached that leaf. The predicted class is the class with the larger proportion.\n"
