    "\n",
    "> **Challenge ahead:** Complete Level 1 first; this optional route adds a harder application of the same reading.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Part 6: XGBoost as Engineered Gradient Boosting\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost stands for **Extreme Gradient Boosting**. It keeps the sequential boosting idea and adds an optimized implementation with regularization, row and column sampling, efficient split search, and strong engineering support.\n",
    "\n",
    "It is not “a decision tree plus more accuracy.” It is an ensemble whose behavior depends on interacting choices such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `n_estimators`;\n",
    "- `learning_rate`;\n",
    "- `max_depth`;\n",
    "- `subsample`;\n",
    "- `colsample_bytree`;\n",
    "- regularization.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same representation, split, validation, and error-cost rules still apply.\n"
   ]
